From 181d0792ec29583e967356787308be5088ba0151 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HelaFaye <dilsha21@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:19:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] bus-noise and pin-glitch: errors on board wires

bus-noise names parts by id and flips bits in their SPI transfers (MOSI and
MISO, while selected) and I2C bytes (both ways) at a rate per bit, in bursts,
and loses I2C ACKs at a rate per addressing; rates change at run time (qom-set
ber/nack), counters (flips, nacks) count what was injected, and a seed makes
it repeatable. The SSI and I2C cores apply it through a pointer on the part.

pin-glitch pulls a pin low for width-us, wired open-drain through a pin-link:
at random (rate a second, Poisson) or on demand (pulse), counted.

Tests: an MCP23017 NACKing and returning wrong data at the rate set, clean
when it's off; ILI9341 ID reads through noise; a glitch that is a falling
edge interrupt, and about the right number of them at random.
